{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["יכסיומו — it should have said יכסיומו (i.e., with a ḥolam), but on account of the first vav with the shureq, the second one comes as well. And likewise: מוצאיו ומובאיו. It should have said מָבוֹאָיו. From בא — מבוא; or from קם — מקום; from לן — מלון; but parallel to מוצאיו he said מובאיו."], :book :exodus, :voice :rashbam, :lang :en, :chapter 15, :notes {0 "The Hebrew comment contains parenthetical and parenthetical-like clarifications (פירוש בחולם, בשורק) that appear to be scribal or editorial glosses; they are rendered inline as transmitted. The phrase בעלילת is translated as 'parallel to' following the sense of the Arabic-derived בעלילה in medieval Hebrew grammatical usage."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:41:33.232719019Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}